SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  COMMENT 03/19/25 - Shawn M Knabel (shawnknabel@gmail.com): the data table is in COMMENT Extension 1, so you can put hdul[1].data to get the table and hdul[1].heCOMMENT ader to get a description of what was done.                             COMMENT     Extension 2 is a table of the average relative uncertainties (statisCOMMENT tical and systematic calculated over three clean stellar libraries [IndoCOMMENT -US, MILES, and XSL], see Knabel et al. 2025 SLACS KCWI data paper)     COMMENT                                                                         END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / binary table extension                         BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     NAXIS1  =                   74 / length of dimension 1                          NAXIS2  =                  341 / length of dimension 2                          PCOUNT  =                    0 / number of group parameters                     GCOUNT  =                    1 / number of groups                               TFIELDS =                   10 / number of table fields                         TTYPE1  = 'PLATE   '                                                            TFORM1  = 'J       '                                                            TTYPE2  = 'FIBERID '                                                            TFORM2  = 'J       '                                                            TTYPE3  = 'MJD     '                                                            TFORM3  = 'J       '                                                            TTYPE4  = 'RA      '                                                            TFORM4  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE5  = 'DEC     '                                                            TFORM5  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE6  = 'VDISP_SMK'                                                           TFORM6  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE7  = 'VDISP_SMK_ERR'                                                       TFORM7  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE8  = 'SDSS_NAME'                                                           TFORM8  = '14A     '                                                            TTYPE9  = 'SN_PER_PIXEL'                                                        TFORM9  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE10 = 'SN_PER_AA'                                                           TFORM10 = 'D       '                                                            EXTNAME = 'DATA    '           / extension name                                 COMMENT 03/19/25 - Shawn Knabel (shawnknabel@gmail.com): I took the vdisp_slacs_COMMENT asb.fits file from TDCOSMO 2024 Milestone paper repository to replace AdCOMMENT am Bolton velocity dispersion measurements for the 341 SLACS lenses. If COMMENT I couldn't find it, I didn't fit it. They will not have necessarily usedCOMMENT  exactly the same fiber id, because some of them have multiple pointingsCOMMENT  (see e.g. J1538 in Knabel 24a). I used pPXF (M. Cappellari) with the clCOMMENT ean XSL DR3 stellar template library (as in TDCOSMO-XIX kinematic methodCOMMENT s paper Knabel & Mozumdar et al. 2025). For a subset of high S/N objectsCOMMENT  (38 of them), XSL was by far preferred in BIC weighting. The wavelengthCOMMENT  range of fitting was 3600-5350A to account for the XSL dichroic. I alsoCOMMENT  included additive polynomial degree 6, and multiplicative degree 2. \ SCOMMENT N_PER_AA is extracted and given in the range 4000-4500A, for helping makCOMMENT e sense of et al. SN_PER_PIXEL was taken in range 3600-6000A and should COMMENT be not really be used. \ Some objects have NaN values for VD but have SNCOMMENT R, which means the fits failed. Others have NaN for VD and for SNR, whicCOMMENT h means I couldn't find them. \You can use astroquery with these plate, COMMENT fiberid and mjd to get exactly the same spectra that I used. I hope thisCOMMENT  helps you if you inherit this table in the future. :)                  END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             