awnknabel@gmail.com): I binned the 341 SLACCOMMENT S candidates in SNR bins of 5-10, 10-15, and > 15.                      COMMENT        I then calculated the average relative statistical and systematicCOMMENT  uncertainties over that bin sample.                             The BesCOMMENT sel correction is just the diagonal multiplied by the sqrt ( (N + 1)/N )COMMENT  where N is the number of libraries (3).                             I aCOMMENT lso give the median signal-to-noise ratio for each bin (as in the SNR_PECOMMENT R_AA given in extension 1).                                             COMMENT 03/19/25 - Shawn M Knabel (shawnknabel@gmail.com): I binned the 341 SLACCOMMENT S candidates in SNR bins of 5-10, 10-15, and > 15.                      COMMENT        I then calculated the average relative statistical and systematicCOMMENT  uncertainties over that bin sample.                             The BesCOMMENT sel correction is just the diagonal multiplied by the sqrt ( (N + 1)/N )COMMENT  where N is the number of libraries (3).                             I aCOMMENT lso give the median signal-to-noise ratio for each bin (as in the SNR_PECOMMENT R_AA given in extension 1).                                             END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  